{title: 614 - Sound the Battle Cry}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #614 • SOUND THE BATTLE CRY • 10.8.11.9.10.9.10.9}
{lyricist: William F- Sherwin}
{composer: William F; Sherwin}
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 614}
{meta: tune SOUND THE BATTLE CRY}
{meta: meter 10.8.11.9.10.9.10.9}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Ab]Sound the battle cry, See! the foe is nigh;
[Db]Raise the [Ab]standard [Eb]high [Ab/Eb]For [Eb]the Lord;
[Bbm]Gird your armor on, Stand firm, every [Eb]one,
[Ab]Rest your cause upon [Db]His holyword.
[Ab]Rouse, then soldiers! [Fm]rally round the banner!
[Ab/Eb]Ready, steady, [Eb7]pass the [Ab]word along;
[Ab]Onward, forward, [Eb7]shout aloud hosanna!
[Cm]Christ is Captain of [Fm]the mightythrong.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Bbm]Rouse, then soldiers!
[Ab]rally round the banner!
[Eb7]Ready, steady, pass the [Ab]word along;
[Ab]Onward, forward, [Fm]shout aloud hosanna!
[Ab/Eb]Christ is Captain [Eb7]of the [Ab]mighty throng.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Ab]Strong to meet the foe,
[Db]Marching [Ab]on we [Eb]go,
[Bbm]While our cause we [Eb]know
[Ab]Must prevail;
[Ab]Shield and [Fm]banner bright,
[Ab/Eb]Gleaming [Eb7]in the [Ab]light,
[Ab]Battling [Eb7]for the [Ab]right,
[Cm]We ne'er [Fm]can fail.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]O Thou God of all,
[Db]Hear [Ab]us when we [Eb]call,
[Bbm]Help us, one and [Eb]all,
[Ab]By Thy [Db]grace;
[Ab]When the [Fm]battle's done,
[Ab/Eb]And the [Eb7]victory [Ab]won,
[Ab]May we [Eb7]wear the [Ab]crown
[Cm]Before [Fm]Thy face.
{end_of_verse}
